Subject: [PATCH] agent: grok compacts by the window it is given (#7203)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Released Grok Build compacts at 85% of context_window and reads no
auto_compact_threshold_percent off a [model."<id>"] table: 1.0.89 and
1.0.91 parse the key and never act on it (0xRichardH's #7203: a table
told 27% sat at 72% of its window un-compacted and first compacted at
the default), so 4f94b8a8's percent never reached the resolver and Long
conversations went nowhere until Grok's own 85% — a 1M model held to
300K compacted near 850K.

- The window is the one knob: grokWindow places it for where Long
  conversations compacts, rounded up so Grok never compacts before that
  size and never over the model's own, where Grok's 85% is the closest
  it can come (300K becomes 352942, 85% of which is 300K).
- magpie writes no auto_compact_threshold_percent of its own: with the
  window placed for it, one of magpie's would move the very compaction
  it names if a Grok that reads it ever ships. One 4f94b8a8 wrote is
  dropped as the tables are rewritten, one the user set stays.
- A [session] percent, the user's for every model, still keeps the
  windows the models' own, and a window equal to the model's whole one
  is a magpie's now (4f94b8a8 gave every model its whole window), so a
  config of that vintage is placed on its next sync.

What was run: gofmt -l on the changed files (nothing); go vet on
darwin/linux nogui and windows, clean; go build, GOOS=windows go build
and GOOS=linux go build -tags nogui, all built; go test -tags nogui
-count=1 -run 'TestGrok' ./internal/agent/ green, and
TestGrokCompactsByTheWindowItIsGiven red without the change (windows
pro 1000000, flash 200000, want 352942 and 200000).

